reason = "LJ-1.541's obligation is `domAt-at-carve` and LJ-1.559 carries the same obligation name and closed GO, so another attempt buys nothing. The two briefs' obligation lines differ only in the probe path: LJ-1.541 names agents/tasks/LJ-1-541/Probe541.agda::domAt-at-carve and LJ-1.559 names agents/tasks/LJ-1-559/Probe559.agda::domAt-at-carve. LJ-1.559 measured its whole chain from nothing at 7.67 s in a trimmed frame, against LJ-1.541's four 1800 s timeouts, and R-42 (written from LJ-1.541's own bisection) explains the difference as a cross-file respelling cost and not a term size. A rewrite of LJ-1.541 as an import-and-bind was dispatched and timed out again at attempt 0, which is why this is a shelve and not a retry."
